{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Abraham listened to My voice</b> — in everything with which I tested him. <b>And he kept My charge</b> — he guarded himself lest any matter come to hand that I had commanded him to keep, and likewise he kept the commandments lest they be transgressed through preoccupation. And ״My statutes״ are commandments that have no rationale, and likewise he kept My Torah lest it be forgotten by him, along the lines of what it says (Deuteronomy 4:9): ״וּשְׁמֹר נַפְשְׁךָ וגו׳ פֶּן תִּשְׁכַּח אֶת הַדְּבָרִים״ and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:28.808869308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}